{"page_id": "olmo_old_scans_math-2_pg65-p1", "markdown": "# CHAP. VI.\n\nTRANSCENDENTAL FUNCTIONS\n\n51\n\nUsing the formula just proved,\n\nd cos u = d sin |\n\n（ラール）= COS\n\n38. Proof of IX, X, XI, and XII. - Differentiting both sides of the equation\n\ntan u = sin u\n\ncos u\n\nand using the formulas just proved for the differentials of sin u and cos u,\n\nd tan u = cos u d sin u - sin u d cos u\n\ncos\" u\n\n_cos? u du + sin? u du cosẠạu\n\n= see? u du.\n\nBy differentiating both sides of the equations\n\n1\n\nsin u'\n\nsec u - cos u\n\ncsc u = sin u\n\nand using the formulas for the differentials of sin u and cos u, we obtain the differentials of cot u, sec u and ese u.\n\nExample 1. y = sin' (x° + 3).\n\nSince\n\nsin? (x2 + 3) = [sin (22 + 3)8,\n\nwe use the formula for u and so get\n\ndy = 2 sin (x2 + 3) d sin (x2 + 3)\n\n= 2 sin (x + 3) cos (x2 + 3) d (x + 3)\n\n= 4 x sin (x + 3) cos (x2 + 3) dx.\n\nEx. 2. y = sec 2 x tan 2 x.\n\nAe = Sce 2 t the\n\ntan 2x + tan 2 x dx sec 2 x\n\n= sec 2 x sec? 2 x (2) + tan-2 x see 2 x tan 2 x (2)\n\n= 2 sec 2 x (sec? 2 x + tan? 2x).\n\nEXERCISES\n\nIn the following exercises show that the derivatives and differentials have the values given:\n\n/1. y = 2 sin 3 x + 3 cos 2 x,\n\ndy = 6 (cos 3 x - sin 2x).", "width": 853, "height": 1378, "blocks": [{"kind": "heading", "text": "CHAP. VI.", "bbox": {"x": 54.56902341236609, "y": 54.54583329853539, "width": 109.13804713804714, "height": 22.966666666666583}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "TRANSCENDENTAL FUNCTIONS", "bbox": {"x": 209.65993251940725, "y": 54.54583332513096, "width": 416.44781144781143, "height": 22.96666666666674}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "51", "bbox": {"x": 758.2222220786196, "y": 51.67499988516663, "width": 34.4646464646465, "height": 22.96666666666674}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Using the formula just proved,", "bbox": {"x": 54.569027769402254, "y": 109.0916662360417, "width": 381.98316498316507, "height": 34.45000000000003}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "d cos u = d